    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Laborer_JR102333": {
      "title": "Laborer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nPerform general indoor and outdoor labor ( e.g. snow removal, loading and unloading trucks, deliveries, move furniture.) Assist grounds personnel with mowing, planting, weeding, pressure washing, trash removal and recycling.  Perform custodial duties to include cleaning offices, buildings, restrooms, sweeping, mopping, waxing floors, windows, walls and entrances. May assist with special events to include set up and removal of tables, chairs, stages and platforms. Assist skilled tradespersons and other workers as required . May train and lead staff and student employees in proper work methods and procedures. Perform related duties as assigned. May perform minor repairs on equipment. May drive vehicles to pick up and deliver equipment or materials. Complete work, time and material usage reports. Perform other duties as assigned by Superintendent/Supervisor. Additional Position Information: Education :    Requires a high school diploma or GED. Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide numbers (including fractions and decimals). Must be able to read and write sentences.    Licenses/Certifications: Valid Ohio Driver’s License. Experience :    Requires a minimum of 6 months work experience in operating grounds maintenance and custodial equipment ( i.e. mower, garden  tractor, snow blower, floor buffer, etc.) Ability to use hand tools and power tools required .    Leadership : No authority or responsibility for the supervision of others, exclusive of students.    Physical Requirements : Extremely strenuous, with frequent physical exertion such as the lifting of very heavy items (100 lbs.) alone or 100+ lbs. with assistance . Deep bending, crawling, climbing and/or working in difficult or cramped positions for extended periods.    Working Conditions : Routine exposure to heat, cold, moisture/wetness, inclement weather, noise, heights and air pollution. May involve exposure to chemical substances, hazards and moving parts.      Laborer – $15.70/hr., after one year $16.17/hr.+ Full Benefits + Pension & Paid Time Off     Competitive Pay & Job Security - $15.70/hr. starting pay, after one year $16.17hr.   State Pension Plan - The university contributes 14% to your retirement, per the union agreement Comprehensive & Affordable Benefits - Low-cost health, dental, vision, life insurance, and disability coverage Paid Time Off - Vacation, Sick leave, and 11 paid holidays (union benefit)   Paid Parental Leave - 20 paid days for maternity/ paternity leave     Tuition Remission - Available for employees and dependents   Consistent Schedule & Overtime Opportunities - Predictable shifts with OT available   Uniform & Tool Allowances - Provided at no cost    Team-Oriented Workplace - Work alongside skilled professionals in a supportive environment   Shift : Tuesday through Saturday 6:00am – 2:30pm. Work schedule is subject to change in accordance with University needs and/or the results of the shift line-up process. Overtime, call-ins, holidays, and/or weekends, emergencies and various shifts may be mandatory based on University need.      Applicant Instructions:   Please complete the on-line application and attach your resume. Application Deadline:  For fullest consideration, apply by September 2, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Union Position :   This is a Union position with a salary Grade of 3 .  Salary determination is subject to the CWA Collective Bargaining Agreement. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Non-Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): Communication Workers of America For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Biomedical-Engineering_JR102868-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nThe Biomedical Engineering (BME) Department at The University of Akron invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track faculty position at Assistant or Associate Professor levels with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Preference will be given to candidates with research interests in macroscale biomechanics, gait analysis, and prosthetic devices. While the primary interest is experimental biomechanics, exceptional candidates with computational biomechanics expertise will also be considered. The successful  candidate is expected to contribute to our core mission in teaching and research, develop an independent, extramurally funded research program, have a passionate interest in teaching and mentorship for undergraduate and graduate students, and  actively participate in the departmental activities .  Candidates should have a doctoral degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related discipline with a biomedical engineering emphasis.  Post-doctoral training for candidates at the Assistant Professor level is preferable but not required.  Applicants at the Associate Professor level are expected to have an active, nationally or internationally recognized research program. The BME  Department has over 160 undergraduate students and offers ABET-accredited B.S. degrees, M.S. degrees in BME, and a Ph.D. degree through the College. Our department emphasizes experiential learning where a majority of the undergraduate students participate in our top-notch co-operative education program, perform undergraduate research, and are also active in regional and national conferences. The BME department offers interdisciplinary research programs with active collaborations within the university, with other institutions, such as the Cleveland Clinic and Northeast Ohio Medical University, and with local industries. Our research has been supported by funding from the NSF, NIH, DoW, AHA, VA, foundations, and industry. For further information please see  https://www.uakron.edu/engineering/BME . Subject to Collective Bargaining Agreement Requirements Additional Position Information: To apply for this position, candidates must complete the on-line application and submit a single PDF file containing: (1) a cover letter, (2) a detailed CV with a complete list of published and accepted papers in peer-reviewed journals and conferences, and funding record, if any, (3) a compelling research vision and agenda that highlights fundable areas the candidate plans to pursue, (4) a teaching statement that includes the applicant's teaching philosophy, identifies core undergraduate/graduate courses that the candidate can teach, and new courses they would develop, and (5) a list of at least three references. Review of applications will begin in fall 2026 and continue until a successful candidate has been identified.  For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact Human Resources at askHR@uakron.edu. Application Deadline: November 19th, 2026. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): American Association of University Professors For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Iron Bones Email: ibones@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
