    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Program-Director--Sonography_JR103356": {
      "title": "Program Director, Sonography",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nEssential Functions: •  Coordinate, administer, and evaluate all clinical education experiences within the Sonography Program. •  Develop, maintain, and strengthen partnerships with clinical affiliates and healthcare organizations. •  Conduct clinical site visits and evaluate the quality and effectiveness of clinical learning environments. •  Monitor student performance and progression in clinical placements and provide guidance, support, and remediation as needed. •  Teach assigned didactic, laboratory, and/or clinical courses in the Sonography curriculum (Fall, Spring, Summer). •  Collaborate with program faculty to develop, revise, and assess curriculum to ensure alignment with accreditation requirements, industry standards, and workforce needs. •  Assist with student recruitment, admissions, orientation, academic advising, retention, and graduation initiatives. •  Maintain accurate records and documentation related to clinical education, student competencies, and program outcomes. •  Support ongoing assessment, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement efforts. •  Participate in accreditation activities, including data collection, reporting, self-study preparation, and compliance with CAAHEP/JRC-DMS standards. •  Contribute to scholarly activities, evidence-based practice initiatives, applied research, and professional service activities consistent with university expectations. •  Serve on departmental, college, and university committees and participate in community and professional outreach activities. •  Collaborate with faculty, clinical preceptors, and healthcare partners to ensure students develop the clinical competencies necessary for professional practice. Additional Position Information: Education: Requires a relevant Bachelor’s Degree.  Licenses/Certifications/Requirements: Current American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography ARDMS credential in Abdominal Sonography certification. Valid Driver's License. Experience: Requires a minimum of 2 years teaching experience and additional ARDMS credentials in other areas such as Obstetrics and Gynecology and Vascular Technology. Program Director experience required.  Experience providing academic advising to undergraduate students required. Experience with accreditation policies and procedures and participation in activities that support programmatic and/or facility accreditation required. Teaching experience using an online/distance learning format required and using course management software (i.e., Brightspace, Blackboard, etc.) required. Experience with course development and assessment required. Experience undertaking evidence-based practice (and/or applied research) initiatives required.  Application Instructions: In order to be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach your resume.   Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience.   Application Deadline: Review of applicants will begin on October 23, 2026. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Professor--Mathematics_JR103323-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nSubject to Collective Bargaining Agreement Requirements The Department of Mathematics at the University of Akron, a state-assisted metropolitan university with approximately 16,000 students, invites applicants for a tenure-track assistant professor position in the mathematics of data science and/or scientific computing. The department has a strong tradition of interdisciplinary research and offers bachelor's and master's degrees in applied mathematics as well as an accelerated 5-year BS/MS program. The department is housed in the College of Engineering and Polymer Science, which offers doctorate degrees in engineering. The successful applicant may have the opportunity to work with students in the Integrated Biosciences Doctoral Program and may also have the opportunity to participate in the DATA+ Institute, a university-wide initiative that connects students, faculty, departments, and external partners across the University of Akron. The job responsibilities include research and teaching at the university level. Preference will be given to candidates with potential for collaboration with members of the department, the College of Engineering and Polymer Science, or across campus. Salary is commensurate with background and experience. Startup funds are available. Applicants must possess a PhD in mathematics or a closely related field by the time of employment and are expected to provide evidence of an active research program as well as evidence of teaching experience and interest in directing student research. Priority will be given to candidates with postdoctoral experience and demonstrated interest in pursuing external funding. Additional Position Information: Application Instructions In order to be considered for this position, please attach the necessary documents: cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, AMS cover sheet, unofficial copy of graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation, at least one of which should address teaching. Any application materials that are requested beyond the CV can be uploaded in the Application Questions 2 of 2 section. Letters of recommendation should be emailed to Dana Nickle-Rodriguez at dnickle@uakron.edu. Application Deadline Review of applications will begin on November 16th, 2026 and continue until the position has been filled. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): American Association of University Professors For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Iron Bones (On Leave) Email: ibones@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Director--Finance-and-Business-Operations---College-of-Health---Human-Sciences_JR103347": {
      "title": "Director, Finance and Business Operations - College of Health & Human Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJob Summary:   Manage the financial operations of CHHS while supporting the strategic plan under the direction of the Dean of the College in concert with the policies and procedures of the University. Essential Functions: - Plans, directs and manages the business affairs of the College of Health and Human Sciences consistent with the mission, goals and expected outcomes based on a thorough knowledge of university policies and procedures as well as accounting and business principles. - Participates in the long term strategic and financial planning and implementation and management of financial, business and administrative systems. - Develops and maintains the college's annual budget including general revenue fund, sales and service, grant and sponsored programs. - At the direction of the Dean, implements and manages overhead costing processes between the Dean's Office and the schools and other business units in the College of Health and Human Sciences. - Creates and oversees the college travel and procurement processes including resource distribution and management. - Consults and advises the Dean, associate deans and school directors on budget and financial matters relevant to college operations, business planning, auditing, and strategic planning. - As this is a support position for the Dean that deals with confidential information, the vast majority of work must be conducted on the physical premises in the College of Health and Human Sciences' Dean's Office (Mary Gladwin Hall 101). Additional Position Information: Education:   Requires a relevant Bachelor's Degree. Master's degree in relevant field required.   Licenses/Certifications/Requirements:   None.     Experience : Requires a minimum of 2 years progressively responsible work experience in budget and fiscal office management, preferably in higher educational setting with extensive knowledge of fund accounting.  Advanced computer skills required, Workday experience in Human Resources and Financials preferred. Prior supervisory experience required.  Budget management, analytical, organizational and goal setting skills required.  Strong verbal and written communications skills required. Intimate knowledge of the administrative workings of the College and The University of Akron (including policies and procedures) preferred. Experience in working directly with the Budget Office, Finance and Administration Office and the Office of Academic Affairs preferred. Incumbent should possess excellent oral and written communication skills, have effective interpersonal relationships, and be an effective team player and builder. Application deadline: Review of applications will begin on October 21, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Application Instructions: In order to be considered for this position, please attach the necessary documents (CV, Cover letter, etc.) FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Carpenter_JR102088-1": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Under general supervision from supervisor performs semi-skilled and unskilled carpentry work. Essential Functions: 30-40% Perform interior and exterior building maintenance repair of rough and finish carpentry work such as remodeling buildings, repairing roofs, installation and repair of ceilings, doors, floors, building and installing rest rooms and other partitions. 20-40% Repair and installation of door openers for ADA compliance. Assist with repair and installation of glass, door closers, locks, other hardware and Plexiglas fixtures along with other glazing systems. Caulks and seals windows, doors, skylights and framework. 15-60% Design, build, repair and installation of furniture such as counters, cabinets, benches and partitions. Fabricates and installs customized/specialty items such as cabinets and moldings. 10% Selects materials, coordinates activity with other trades, cleans and removes trash, and maintains shop equipment and vehicles. 10% Secures unprotected openings (windows, doors) until next workday (call-ins, emergencies). 0-10% Complete work, time and material usage reports. Perform other duties as assigned by superintendent/supervisor. Additional Position Information: Education : Requires high school diploma or GED. Licenses/Certifications : Valid Ohio Driver’s License. Experience : Requires completion of a 2-year University of Akron or other State Approved Sponsored Apprenticeship Program for Trade OR a minimum 5 years of carpenter trades experience. Ability to operate and use standard powered and nonpowered carpentry tools and equipment such as hammers, saws, screwdrivers, drills, chisels, table saws, routers and surface planers required. Ability to perform mathematics associated with trade applications (fractions, ratios, percentages) required. Ability to read, write and accurately follow oral, written and graphic instructions required. Must be able to interpret drawings and blueprints. Leadership : Responsible for directing and monitoring the work of student and/or temporary workers. Physical Requirements : Must be able to lift 80 pounds without assistance and demonstrate bending, crouching and lifting. Must be able to climb a ladder, scaffolding and work on rooftops. Working Conditions: Routine exposure to heat, cold, moisture/wetness, inclement weather and noise. May involve exposure to chemical substances, hazards and moving parts. Overtime/call-ins may be mandatory based on University needs. Carpenter– $21.54/hr., after one year $22.20/hr.+ Full Benefits + Pension & Paid Time Off   Competitive Pay & Job Security- $21.54/hr., after one year $22.20/hr. State Pension Plan - The university contributes 14% to your retirement, per the union agreement. Comprehensive & Affordable Benefits - Low-cost health, dental, vision, life insurance, and disability coverage. Paid Time Off - Vacation, Sick leave, and 11 paid holidays (union benefit). Paid Parental Leave - 20 paid days for maternity/paternity leave. Tuition Remission - Available for employees and dependents. Consistent Schedule & Overtime Opportunities - Predictable shifts with OT available. Uniform & Tool Allowances - Provided at no cost. Team-Oriented Workplace - Work alongside skilled professionals in a supportive environment. Shift available:  Mon - Fri, 7:00am - 3:30am with days off Sat and Sun. Learn more about benefits at The University of Akron: https://www.uakron.edu/hr/benefits/     Application Instructions : In order to be considered for this position, please submit an online application and attach your resume. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Non-Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): Communication Workers of America For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
