    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Director--Academic-Success-Program_JR103060": {
      "title": "Director, Academic Success Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Teach relevant law courses to students. Responsible for the design, delivery, and continuous improvement of academic success programs for law students across all years. Counsel and support students by conducting workshops.  Provide strategic leadership in skills-based teaching, support students by counseling and tutoring, and create early intervention initiatives that promote academic excellence, retention, and bar readiness.  Demonstrate commitment to student development, and collaborative academic support practices tailored to diverse learning styles and student needs including basic writing and analytic skills. Essential Functions: Develop and manage a comprehensive academic success program spanning first-year through upper-division law students. Teach academic success courses (e.g., Advanced Legal Applications and Foundations of Law) and deliver skills-based workshops (e.g., legal analysis, exam writing, time management).  Provide individualized academic counseling and coaching to students, including those identified as at-risk. Supervise and train academic success fellows, student assistants, and peer tutors in delivering effective support. Utilize technology innovations to enhance students’ learning experience Design and implement early assessment tools and data-driven interventions to improve student outcomes. Collaborate with Academic Success Faculty to recruit, coordinate, train, and supervise ASP student fellows.  to integrate academic skills instruction into the broader law school curriculum. Track student performance metrics and provide reports to administration on academic trends and outcomes. Serve on committees focused on academic achievement, retention, and curriculum development as needed.  Work in close coordination with the Director of Bar Success to ensure alignment between academic and bar-readiness efforts. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Dean, Associate Dean or Professor of Academic Success. Additional Position Information: Education: Requires a Juris Doctorate Degree. Licenses/Certifications/Requirements: Law Licensure Experience: Requires a minimum of 2 years of demonstrated successful teaching experience, preferably in areas such as academic success, bar preparation, legal skills, or legal writing. Strong computer skills (including spreadsheet, word processing, and database capabilities) are required.  Preferred Qualifications: A demonstrated record of effective self-starting and follow-through is preferred. Demonstrated success in assisting student learning with the ability to identify methods to enhance learning for multiple learning styles is preferred.  The ability to build rapport with all students, including those at risk, and a demonstrated ability to work well with a variety of constituencies are preferred.  The ability to create, implement, and evaluate academic support is preferred. Leadership: Responsible for directing and monitoring the work of students and/or temporary workers. Physical Requirements: Job is physically comfortable;  individual is normally seated and has discretion about walking, standing, etc.  May occasionally lift very lightweight objects. Working Conditions: No major sources of working conditions discomfort, standard working environment with possible minor inconveniences due to   occasional noise, crowded working conditions, minor heating/cooling or ventilation problems, and/or up to 40% use of PC terminal. Application Instructions: In order to be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach your resume. Please note that you can add other documents to this list that your department requires, such as a cover letter, 3 professional references, and official transcripts, etc. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on August 6, 2026. Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Associate-Director--Fraternity---Sorority-Life_JR103194": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Fraternity & Sorority Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nEssential Functions: Characteristic duties and responsibilities of the Associate Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life (FSL) include:  Advise the Panhellenic, National Pan-Hellenic & Interfraternity Councils; advise individual fraternity and sorority chapters; advise Gamma Sigma Alpha, Ordre of Omega & Rho Lambda  Assist organizations in developing, coordinating and upholding policies and procedures; establish specialized training & personalized assistance to organizations; maintain accurate records of chapter membership, recruitment statistics, service hours, and scholarship; management of Office RooConnect page, including update of forms, files and resources  Supervise and provide an educational experience to two (2) student staff within the Office of Fraternity and Sorority Life  Assist in the programming of key fraternity and sorority life events and traditions; lead effective and comprehensive recruitment activities and initiatives  Serve as a resource for faculty, staff, students, alumni/ae and national offices that collaborate and support fraternity and sorority initiatives.  Provide professional development by serving on University committees and being involved in various organizations.  Coordinate educational programs geared toward the fraternity and sorority community with a special emphasis on recruitment, community, & policy.   Handle contract negotiation and processing as it pertains to programs & events.  Manage programming budget by planning, directing, and controlling the financial   Manage the FSL Enhancement Fund by administering chapter recruitment grants, supporting professional development initiatives, overseeing the FSL Ambassadors program, and ensuring strategic use of gift funds to strengthen and grow the FSL community.  Lead collaborative efforts with the University Alumni Association to strengthen engagement with fraternity and sorority alumni by coordinating meetings, and developing strategies that enhance alumni involvement, mentorship, philanthropy, and support of the FSL community  Develop and implementing marketing strategies for fraternity and sorority life programs  Develop an ongoing assessment program (qualitative & quantitative) to monitor the satisfaction with and growth of fraternity and sorority life programming  Oversees the Department of Student Life Marketing area; supervising a team of student employees including a social media coordinator, 2-3 student photographers, and a content creator, to create engaging content and promote department programs and events across digital and social media platforms  Assist Director, Student Life with special projects and perform other duties as assigned  Additional Position Information: Education: Requires a relevant master's degree. Experience: Requires a minimum of 2 years' experience with fraternity and sorority life programs, advising, and/or employment with a national fraternity or sorority required. Ability to counsel and advise students regarding university policies and requirements required. Strong organizational, written and oral communications skills required. Demonstrated leadership ability required. An articulate understanding of the mission, culture, climate and environment of a metropolitan university required. Experience with Workday and Microsoft Office preferred  Leadership: Direct supervision and evaluation of work as a first-line supervisor over non-exempt staff including hiring, terminating, disciplining; or functional guidance and/or project leadership over exempt staff engaged in activities of a recurring basis. Physical Requirements: Job is physically comfortable; individual is normally seated and has discretion about walking, standing, etc. May occasionally lift very lightweight objects. Working Conditions: No major sources of working conditions discomfort, standard working environment with possible minor inconveniences due to occasional noise, crowded working conditions, minor heating/cooling or ventilation problems, and/or up to 40% use of PC terminal. Application Instructions: In order to be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach your resume. Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience. Application Deadline: For best consideration, apply by October 13, 2026 . Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Natasha Kuzmina Email: nkuzmina@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UACareers/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Building-Services-Worker_JR100012": {
      "title": "Assistant Building Services Worker - Custodial",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nAn Assistant Building Services Worker position involves performing custodial and maintenance duties to ensure the cleanliness and upkeep of buildings, furniture, and fixtures. Responsibilities include cleaning and maintaining floors, carpets, furniture, restrooms, and common areas; emptying trash; stocking supplies; and removing snow and ice from walkways. Work is carried out under general supervision across classrooms, offices and other campus facilities. This is a Union position for which The Communications Workers of America has been designated as the exclusive representative. We are actively hiring and have multiple positions available. This position involves shift work, and the shift will be selected for the employee based on university needs.  Current vacancies available on  second and third shift , opportunities available for this position. Sunday – Thursday from 11:00 PM – 7:30 AM, Monday – Friday, 11:00 PM – 7:30 AM, Sunday – Thursday 3:00 PM – 11:30 PM, and Tuesday – Saturday 3:00 PM – 11:30 PM Additional Position Information: Assistant Building Services Worker – $15.00/hr., after one year $15.43/hr.+ Full Benefits + Pension & Paid Time Off. Competitive Pay & Job Security- $15.00/hr. starting pay, after one year $15.43hr., structured union increases, and year-round employment. State Pension Plan - The university contributes 14% to your retirement, per the union agreement. Comprehensive & Affordable Benefits - Low-cost health, dental, vision, life insurance, and disability coverage. Paid Time Off - Vacation, Sick leave, and 11 paid holidays (union benefit). Paid Parental Leave - 20 paid days for maternity/paternity leave. Tuition Remission - Available for employees and dependents. Consistent Schedule & Overtime Opportunities - Predictable shifts with OT available. Uniform & Tool Allowances - Provided at no cost. Team-Oriented Workplace - Work alongside skilled professionals in a supportive environment.   Learn more about benefits at The University of Akron: https://www.uakron.edu/hr/benefits/   Application Deadline: Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis and review will continue until all vacancies are filled. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, you must complete the online application and attach a list of three professional references with contact information. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Non-Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): Communication Workers of America For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
